# MARLEY reaction data for charged current ve on 56Fe
# Revised 14 August 2020 by Sam Hedges
#
# Particle IDs conform to the 2017 revision of the
# Particle Data Group Monte Carlo Particle Numbering Scheme
# (see http://pdg.lbl.gov/2018/reviews/rpp2018-rev-monte-carlo-numbering.pdf)
#
# B(GT) values for levels in 56Co from 15.7 MeV and below were taken from J.
# Rapaport, et al., Nucl. Phys. A 410, 3 (1983) as provided within N. Paar, et al.,
# Intern. Jour. of Mod. Phys. E 24, 09 (2015). The lowest two energy levels were
# assumed to correspond to levels within ENSDF compiled by Huo Junde, Huo Su, and
# Yang Dong, NDS 112, 1513 (2009). That publication corresponds to the ENSDF data
# (https://www.nndc.bnl.gov/ensdf/) for 56Co. Experimental values were multiplied
# by g_A^2 = (1.26)^2 to account for their differing definition of B(GT), which did
# not include that weak axial-vector coupling constant. Above 15.7 MeV, the
# RNEDF (DD-ME2) RQRPA results were used with gaussian fits to the distribution to
# identify B(GT) strength at discrete excitation energies. The RQRPA calculations were
# multiplied by g_A^2 = (1.262)^2 to account for the differing definition of B(GT).
#
# The B(F) value was taken as the sum-rule value g_V^2*(N_i - Z_i) with g_V=1
#
# Particle IDs and final ion charge
0 1000260560 0
